the product catalog itself.

00:13:38.560 --> 00:13:40.690
So we help you
track that as well.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:42.250
Because obviously,
if you send us

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:44.542
a product ID that doesn't
exist in the product catalog,

00:13:44.542 --> 00:13:46.480
then we can't do
anything with it.

00:13:46.480 --> 00:13:49.890
So you can track
that here as well.

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:51.320
And then also one
of the benefits

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:54.740
of being part of
Google Cloud Platform

00:13:54.740 --> 00:13:58.940
is that there are all sorts of
other systems for maintaining

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:02.730
production systems that we
can be natively integrated to.

00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:06.740
So for example, you can
check your API metrics here.

00:14:06.740 --> 00:14:09.800
People especially care about
the latency and the error rate

00:14:09.800 --> 00:14:13.992
of their predict method in terms
of retrieving recommendations.

00:14:13.992 --> 00:14:15.200
So you can monitor that here.

00:14:18.020 --> 00:14:22.530
I'm going to set it to that
filter to the predict API

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:23.370
method.

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.890
And you can see
the total traffic,

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:32.050
the errors that are happening,
the latency of these calls.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.550
So obviously, a lot of you
want to keep the recommender

00:14:35.550 --> 00:14:38.340
at the 95th percentile
within 150 milliseconds,

00:14:38.340 --> 00:14:40.740
just to make sure it's a
highly dynamic experience.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:46.740
So you can check that at any
time, as well as more detailed

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:47.490
latency view here.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:53.900
Next, you can go over individual
errors that you've hit.

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:59.600
So this is also a common issue
where people send poor data.

00:14:59.600 --> 00:15:03.100
So we can allow you to deep
dive on what the errors are.

00:15:03.100 --> 00:15:05.860
And finally, one
of the big things

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:08.770
in terms of making sure the
recommender is making money

00:15:08.770 --> 00:15:11.915
for you day in and
day out, is you

00:15:11.915 --> 00:15:14.290
have to actually make sure
it's working on a daily basis.

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:16.180
But you don't want to
look at the dashboard

00:15:16.180 --> 00:15:17.650
every single day, right?

00:15:17.650 --> 00:15:21.590
So if you want to avoid that,
you can also set up alerting.

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:26.380
So here, for example,
in this demo project,

00:15:26.380 --> 00:15:30.550
we've set up an alert for when
the predict errors is above 0.

00:15:30.550 --> 00:15:33.130
So if there's ever some
kind of system problem

00:15:33.130 --> 00:15:34.960
that causes the
pipeline to break,

00:15:34.960 --> 00:15:37.240
then you can be
alerted without you

00:15:37.240 --> 00:15:39.580
having to look at the
dashboard every day.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.430
So all sorts of
functionality to ensure

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:44.710
that your recommender is
making money for you day in

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:45.920
and day out.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.790
So on top of having state of the
art models and recommendation

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:51.030
techniques.

00:15:51.030 --> 00:15:54.320
If we go back to the slides.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:57.470
And finally, since these
questions always get asked,

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:00.440
I wanted to let you know
upfront that you can rest easy.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:02.660
So your data isn't used
for any other Google

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:04.100
customer or Google product.

00:16:04.100 --> 00:16:07.203
It just belongs to you and
it sits inside your project.

00:16:07.203 --> 00:16:09.620
Your data isn't mixed with
that of other Google customers.

00:16:09.620 --> 00:16:11.328
We don't mix all the
user events together

00:16:11.328 --> 00:16:12.530
and create one master model.

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.600
There's one model
per customer that we

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.340
will train on a daily basis.

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:19.650
You always can delete your
data and models at any time.

00:16:19.650 --> 00:16:21.570
This is a commonly
asked question.

00:16:21.570 --> 00:16:23.660
And finally, we support
GDPR compliance.

